this is devante chisholm reading for  jordan remay and gabe gerwin assassin's  creed valhalla's main story may take  around 60 hours to complete but that  doesn't mean avora's adventures are done  just yet dawn of ragnarok the game's  newest dlc is a 35-hour adventure that  sees avor stepping into the shoes of  odin once more and changes the  assassin's creed formula in fun new ways  here's everything you need to know about  assassin's creed valhalla dawn of  ragnarok  in ac valhalla the asgard and jodenheim  sagas conclude with javi aka odin  learning that there's no way for them to  physically survive ragnarok however they  can undergo an experimental procedure to  be born again that's where assassin's  creed sages come from we come to  discover the sages are actually isu from  javi's time that go on to be reborn as  humans knowing that they and their  allies will be reborn following ragnarok  javi faces the coming end of the world  and donna ragnarok picks up there with  hobbies seeking out their son balder who  has been kidnapped and imprisoned within  the realm of dwarves a land that has  been consumed by war ahead of ragnarok  javi's quest will see them once again  face the frost giants of jodenheim but  this time they'll go up against a more  fiery foe sirder though the expansion  takes place after the events of asgard  and jodenheim sagas you'll be able to  jump into donna ragnarok even if you  haven't completed those storylines the  developer ubisoft sophia told gamespot  that it has taken special care to make  sure that new players will be just as  engaged with the narrative as those that  have completed valhalla adding to this  when we asked the ubisoft montreal why  donna ragnarok was made dlc instead of a  standalone title it responded quote the  team has made efforts to make all  content be more accessible to players  expansions included so they can explore  the world of valhalla not unlike a theme  park we wanted players to be able to  choose which saga they embark on be it  england ireland frankia and now the  realm of dwarves expansions one and two  focused more on the viking facet of  valhalla and explored avor as a  character under different circumstances  now dawn of ragnarok feels like the  other side of the coin where we go  deeper into the north mythology and more  so into odin slash hobby's backstory the  studio went on to say quote given how  important north mythology was to the  vikings everyday life we felt donna  ragnarok needed to be included in  assassin's creed valhalla  in this game you'll be exploring the  mythical dwarven realm of sfarthelheim a  region that's only accessible via volca  raventhorpe's seer in a similar manner  to asgard and jodenheim in the game's  main campaign this land historically  said to be ruled by dwarves has seen the  native community scattered into hiding  spots to avoid destruction and forced  labor ubisoft's sophia has avoided the  common trope of having buff bearded  dudes with scottish accents for this  role instead depicting the dwarves as a  slightly smaller human-like race the dev  also noted that ragnarok's map is  one-third the size of valhalla's england  [Music]  in dawn of ragnarok odin has a number of  special abilities that weren't available  during valhalla's other mythical  excursions acquirable through a new  skill tree these abilities include the  power of the raven which lets odin  temporarily turn into a bird to quickly  scale mountains or get the drop on  enemies as well as the appearance  changing power of muskelheim  another one of these abilities is power  of rebirth a skill that when activated  temporarily turns anyone odin kills into  an ally use it at an opportune time such  as when you're facing an enormous number  of enemies and you can change the fight  from being a lost cause into an all-out  slaughter in your favor  you do have to choose carefully though  however as only a few of these abilities  can be equipped at a time their use is  also tied to a new resource hooger which  you can get from enemies certain objects  in the environment and shrines though  the latter option requires a sacrifice  of health in order to do so  it always provides  this give and take balancing of these  powers looks like it will be most  interesting in dawn of ragnarok's combat  arenas these gauntlets provide extra  challenges in exchange for ever  increasing rewards tied to their  difficulty ubisoft sophia told gamespot  quote we wanted to really make a  difference in all players gameplay no  matter if they like face-to-face combat  stealthily taking out the opposition  exploring the realm of dwarves in search  of the dwarves ancient secrets and  mystery or solving puzzles to get the  valuable treasure the powers let odin  reach inaccessible locations give them  new stealth opportunities let them  traverse the world in a different manner  and lay devastation on the forces of  jodenheim and muspelheim alongside the  mythical abilities odin also has an  entirely new weapon type in dawn of  ragnarok the atgire based on the  viking's own spear but resembling  something out of monster hunter it's a  powerful two-handed weapon with its own  combo system it's also capable of  delivering powerful blows into the  ground as well as swift attacks to take  out several enemies  did my tale please you valkyrie donna  ragnarok is coming from ubisoft sophia  the lead studio for assassin's creed iii  liberation assassin's creed rogue and  assassin's creed origins the curse of  the prophets dlc guiles armstrong is  senior scriptwriter for donna ragnarok  and his work includes being lead writer  on destruction all-stars and a writer  for marvel's guardians of the galaxy  assassin's creed valhalla dawn of  ragnarok releases on ps4 ps5 xbox one  xbox series x and s stadia and pc on  march 10. and even though it's the size  of a full game this is still considered  dlc and will only cost you 40 bucks 15  more than wrath of the druids and the  siege of paris and there you have it  everything you need to know about  assassin's creed valhalla dawn of  ragnarok  if you're excited to play this massive  expansion make sure to let us know in  the comments below we'll have more  videos about the game once it launches  including our review so make sure you  subscribe so you get notified when it  becomes available  gentlemen  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

